{"id":"d05f6a48eb0cb4022dcfda6bc0440c7613b9ef63b693eab40f7a390276ad7383","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T19:58:00.833194118Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nA single `ti sync` (ti 0.4.1) in a repo with one author and unsynced local work lost data that existed only locally, and brought back tickets that had been deleted locally. Nothing on the remote was newer than the last push as far as I can tell (not verified: the pre-sync remote ref was overwritten).\n\n## What happened\n\nSync ran at 2026-11-08 19:47:31 UTC. The previous sync was 11:34 UTC (backup ref `refs/ticgit-backup/meta/1794167251-30c9aee0` holds that state). Local work between the two syncs was lost or damaged:\n\n1. **Comments dropped.** Two comments pushed to ticket A (19:13:39 and 19:31:15) and at least one pushed to ticket B (19:31:15) were gone after the sync. The original text could not be recovered from the DB; I rewrote ticket A's from my notes. The log shows a `set` on the `comments` key of A and B at 19:47:31 (the merge rewrote the whole list). Ticket C also got a comment at 19:31:15, had no `set` at sync time, and kept it.\n2. **Set members tombstoned.** Six `set_member` tombstones were written at 19:47:31 (timestamp 1794167251635) for entries added locally at 19:13:39 and never synced: two `children` entries on the map ticket (two sub-issues created at 19:13:28) and four `depends_on` entries. Net effect: two new sub-issues disappeared from the map's `ti show` and four dependency edges vanished. The tickets themselves, and their `parent` field, were intact.\n3. **Deleted tickets came back.** Two tickets deleted locally before the sync reappeared. Their `ops/*` and `format-version` rows were in the previous backup, so the remote still had them. The log has `rm` and `set` rows for those ops at 19:47:31.\n4. **No CLI repair path.** With the `parent` field set but the parent's `children` set missing the child, `ti subissue <parent> -t <child>` and `ti subissue --clear -t <child>` both fail with:\n\n```\ngit-meta error: value not found: '<child-id>' not found in set\n```\n\nBoth try to remove the child from the set first. I repaired it by deleting the two tombstone rows and inserting the two `set_values` rows into `.git/git-meta.sqlite` by hand.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Sync merges remote and local without dropping local-only list entries or set members.\n- A deletion is a tombstone that wins over an older remote copy, or sync warns about the conflict.\n- Re-linking a sub-issue works whenever `parent` and the `children` set disagree.\n\n## Not yet known\n\n- Whether the remote had changed since the previous sync. If it had not, even a no-op pull lost local-only data.\n- Why comments on one ticket were rewritten (`set`) and another's were not.\n- Not reproduced from a clean repo. A repro would be: create tickets, comments, a sub-issue link and a delete locally after a sync, then `ti sync` against a remote that holds the previous state.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- ti 0.4.1.\n- `.git/git-meta.sqlite`: the `metadata_log` table has the 19:47:31 `set` and `rm` rows, and `tombstones` has the six rows at timestamp 1794167251635.\n- Serialized tree: `git diff --stat 30c9aee ea6a4b4` on `refs/meta/local/main` shows only added files, so history was not rewritten; the loss happened in the merge into the local DB before serialization."}}}